{
  "id": "T03",
  "title": "Medication reconciliation for a single visit day",
  "scenario": "During medication reconciliation for a clinic visit on 2024-06-15, an app queries MedicationStatement to find what the patient was taking around that day. Statements have open-ended periods, periods with only an end, day- and month-precision bounds, UTC instants and one statement with no effective value.",
  "server_timezone": "America/New_York",
  "why_hard": "Period end dates at day precision cover the whole end day (end '2024-06-15' reaches 2024-06-16T04:00Z), a missing start is -infinity and a missing end is +infinity, ge+le together mean 'overlaps' while eq means 'contained', sa/eb need strict separation, and :missing applies only to the effective value. A minute-precision eq search contains only values that fit inside that minute.",
